pecifier (e.g. *al-wālid* = the father, *aṭ-ṭālib* = the student).\n     * **RULE 3:** It takes the **Genitive Case (al-Majrūr)**, marked by a **kasra (-i)** or genitive ending!\n\n2. **Concrete Examples:**\n   - 'The father's house' / 'The house of the father':\n     * **بَيْتُ الوَالِدِ** (*baytu al-wālidi* [BAY-too al-WAH-lee-dee])\n     * (Notice: *baytu* has no 'al-' and no tanwīn; *al-wālidi* ends with genitive kasra!).\n   - 'The teacher's car':\n     * **سَيَّارَةُ المُعَلِّمِ** (*sayyāratu al-muʿallimi*)\n   - 'The university library':\n     * **مَكْتَبَةُ الجَامِعَةِ** (*maktabatu al-jāmiʿati*)\n   - 'My sister's book':\n     * **كِتَابُ أُخْتِي** (*kitābu ukhtī*)\n\n3. **Indefinite Iḍāfa:**\n   - If Term 2 is indefinite (with tanwīn kasr -in), the entire phrase is indefinite:\n     * **بَيْتُ رَجُلٍ** (*baytu rajulin* = a house of a man / a man's house).",
