er's sister)\n- **اِبْنُ خَالِي** (ibnu khālī) — My male maternal cousin\n- **بِنْتُ خَالَتِي** (bintu khālatī) — My female maternal cousin\n\n3. **Grandparents & Spouses:**\n- **جَدّ** (jadd [JAHDD]) — Grandfather\n- **جَدَّة** (jaddah [JAH-dah]) — Grandmother\n- **حَفِيد** (ḥafīd [hah-FEED]) — Grandson\n- **حَفِيدَة** (ḥafīdah [hah-FEE-dah]) — Granddaughter\n- **زَوْج** (zawj [ZOWJ]) — Husband\n- **زَوْجَة** (zawjah [ZOW-jah]) — Wife\n\n4. **Root Etymology & Cultural Precision:**\n- *ʿAmm* derives from the root **ع-م-م (ʿ-M-M)** denoting commonality, inclusion, and paternal clan leadership.\n- *Khāl* derives from the root **خ-و-ل (Kh-W-L)** denoting maternal care, protection, and nurturing.",
