(*Aṭ-ṭālibu yadrusu al-'arabiyyata* = The student, he studies Arabic).\n\n3. **THE FAMOUS MSA SUBJECT-VERB AGREEMENT RULE (Crucial Law!):**\n- **Rule 1 (VSO - Verb FIRST):** When the verb comes **BEFORE** a plural human subject, the verb **REMAINS SINGULAR in number** (matching only the gender!):\n  * **يَدْرُسُ الطُّلابُ فِي المَكْتَبَة.** (*Yadrusu [singular verb!] aṭ-ṭullābu [plural subject!] fī al-maktaba* = The students study in the library).\n  * (❌ NEVER say 'Yadrusūna aṭ-ṭullābu' in standard written Arabic!).\n  * Feminine: **تَدْرُسُ الطَّالِبَاتُ.** (*Tadrusu aṭ-ṭālibātu* = The female students study).\n- **Rule 2 (SVO - Subject FIRST):** When the subject comes **BEFORE** the verb, the verb **MUST FULLY AGREE in both gender AND plural number**:\n  * **الطُّلابُ يَدْرُسُونَ فِي المَكْتَبَة.** (*Aṭ-ṭullābu yadrusūna [plural verb!] fī al-maktaba*).",
