 wrote), **رَجَعْنَ** (*rajaʿna* - They f. returned).\n\n2. Sentence Word Order Agreement Rule (VSO vs. SVO):\n   - **SVO (Subject First)**: The verb agrees in number and gender with the plural subject:\n     - *الطُّلَّابُ ذَهَبُوا إِلَى المُتْحَفِ.* (*Aṭ-ṭullābu dhahabū 'ilā al-matḥaf.* - The students went to the museum.)\n   - **VSO (Verb First)**: The verb stays **SINGULAR** (matching only gender!):\n     - *ذَهَبَ الطُّلَّابُ إِلَى المُتْحَفِ.* (*Dhahaba aṭ-ṭullābu...* - Went the students to the museum.)",
