 (*kunnā* - We were)\n   - **With He/She/They**: The long vowel stays! **كَانَ** (*kāna* - he was), **كَانَتْ** (*kānat* - she was), **كَانُوا** (*kānū* - they were).\n\n2. Defective Verbs (الفِعْل النَّاقِص - Final Weak Letter):\n   - **رَأَى** (*ra'ā* - he saw) -> **رَأَيْتُ** (*ra'aytu* - I saw), **رَأَيْنَا** (*ra'aynā* - we saw).\n   - **مَشَى** (*mashā* - he walked) -> **مَشَيْتُ** (*mashaytu* - I walked), **مَشَيْنَا** (*mashaynā* - we walked).\n   - **حَكَى** (*ḥakā* - he spoke/narrated) -> **حَكَيْتُ** (*ḥakaytu* - I spoke).",
