īlan wa-baʿḍa at-tawābili wa-al-ʿuṭūr. Wa-baʿda dhālik, 'akalnā kushan miṣriyyan ladhīdhan!* - Yes, I bought a beautiful brass lamp and some spices and perfumes. After that, we ate delicious Egyptian koshari!)\n   - **طَارِق**: يَالَهُ مِنْ يَوْمٍ جَمِيلٍ! أَنَا أَيْضاً كُنْتُ فِي الجِيزَةِ وَرَأَيْتُ الأَهْرَامَاتِ. (*Yā lahu min yawmin jamīl! 'Anā 'ayḍan kuntu fī al-Jīzah wa-ra'aytu al-'ahrāmāt.* - What a beautiful day! I was also in Giza and saw the Pyramids.)",
