nder / below (*taḥta al-'arḍ = underground*)\n   - **قَرِيبٌ مِنْ** (qarībun min) = near to / close to (*qarīb min al-maḥaṭṭah*)\n   - **بَعِيدٌ عَنْ** (ba'īdun 'an) = far from (*ba'īd 'an wasaṭ al-madīnah*).\n\n2. Genitive Governance Rule (الْمَجْرُور بِالْإِضَافَة):\n   - The noun following any locative adverb ('amāma, khalfa, bayna, etc.) functions as the second term of an iḍāfa (mudāf 'ilayhi) and is **always in the genitive case (Majrūr with kasrah -i)**:\n     - *'amāma al-masjid**i*** (in front of the mosque)\n     - *bijānib al-mustashfā* (next to the hospital)\n     - *bayna al-shāri'ayn**i*** (between the two streets).",
