u wāsiʿatun = *'The room IS spacious.'*)\n\n2. The 4 Dimensions of Adjective Agreement:\n   - **Gender**: Masc. noun $\\rightarrow$ Masc. adj (*بَيْتٌ جَدِيدٌ*); Fem. noun (ends in ة) $\\rightarrow$ Fem. adj (*شَقَّةٌ جَدِيدَةٌ*).\n   - **Number**: Singular $\\rightarrow$ Singular.\n   - **Case**: Ḍamma in nominative sentences (*مَرْفُوع*).\n   - **The Non-Human Plural Rule (قَاعِدَةُ جَمْعِ غَيْرِ العَاقِل)**:\n     - *ALL non-human plural nouns are treated as SINGULAR FEMININE for adjectives!*:\n     - *غُرَفٌ جَمِيلَةٌ* (ghurafun jamīlatun = beautiful rooms - *jamīla is singular feminine!*)\n     - *بُيُوتٌ قَدِيمَةٌ* (buyūtun qadīmatun = old houses).",
