; actors planted among the audience interrupt an official state play, demanding truth and confronting authoritarian failure;\n  - **«مغامرة رأس المملوك جابر» (The Adventure of the Mamluk Jaber's Head - 1970)**: Staged through a traditional café Hakawati storyteller, exposing how cowardly self-preservation leads to decapitation;\n  - **«طقوس الإشارات والتحولات» (Rituals of Signs and Transformations - 1994)**;\n  - **The 1996 World Theatre Day Address**: Delivered to UNESCO while dying of cancer, concluding with the immortal words that inspire the Arab world: **«إننا محكومون بالأمل، وما يحدث اليوم لا يمكن أن يكون نهاية التاريخ»** (We are doomed to hope, and what is happening today cannot be the end of history).",
