a)**:\n  - Follows two universal archetypes: **Farfur (الفرفور)**, the quick-witted, rebellious peasant jester, and **El-Sayyid (السيد)**, the authoritarian master looking for an identity;\n  - Explores the existential master-slave dialectic (*Who created whom?*);\n  - Climax: In death, both Farfur and the Master become equal subatomic particles spinning in the universe, realizing that human freedom is impossible without universal equality.",
