 من الاتصال» (The Decisive Treatise - 1179)**:\n    - Proved that rational philosophical inquiry (*Hikma*) is not forbidden in Islam, but rather an **explicit religious obligation commanded by the Qur'an** (quoting: *«فَاعْتَبِرُوا يَا أُولِي الْأَبْصَارِ»* / \"Reflect, O you who possess vision\");\n    - Formulated the Principle of Harmony: **\"Truth cannot contradict truth\" (الحق لا يضاد الحق)**—rational demonstration and divine revelation are two harmonious paths arriving at the same ultimate reality;\n  - **«تهافت التهافت» (The Incoherence of the Incoherence)**: Defended rational causation and universal philosophy against Al-Ghazali's critiques;\n  - **«بداية المجتهد ونهاية المقتصد»**: Foundational comparative Islamic jurisprudence.",
