e perception (the eye sees a star as small as a coin, while geometry proves it larger than Earth); then doubted rational mathematics (could waking life be a dream from which we will awake upon death?);\n    - Discovered that ultimate metaphysical certainty is not attained through cold syllogisms alone, but through **\"a light which God cast into the breast\" (نور قذفه الله في الصدر)**;\n  - **«تهافت الفلاسفة» (The Incoherence of the Philosophers)**: Rigorous critique of Neoplatonic metaphysics and Aristotelian determinism, proving that causal connections are not necessary intrinsic properties of matter, but continuous divine custom (*Iqtiran*);\n  - **«إحياء علوم الدين» (The Revival of the Religious Sciences)**: 40-volume spiritual masterwork revitalizing ethics, psychology, and inner devotion.",
