e bustling chaos of Cairo's Ramses Railway Station, obsessing over the soda seller Hanuma (Hind Rostom);\n  - **«الأرض» (The Earth - 1969)**: Epic agrarian masterpiece about Egyptian peasant farmers (*Fellahin*) fighting to defend their ancestral irrigation water against feudal landlords, culminating in Mahmud al-Meliguy's hands clinging to the mud;\n  - **The Autobiographical Alexandria Quartet**:\n    - **«إسكندرية... ليه؟» (Alexandria... Why? - 1978 - Berlin Silver Bear)**: Nostalgic portrait of cosmopolitan Alexandria during WWII;\n    - **«المصير» (Destiny - 1997)**: Historical epic on philosopher Ibn Rushd (Averroës) in Córdoba, carrying the defiant anti-extremist motto: **«الأفكار لها أجنحة، لا يستطيع أحد أن يمنعها من الطيران»** (*\"Ideas have wings; no one can stop them from flying\"*).",
