ned with refractory clay or stone, preheated with glowing aromatic desert hardwood charcoal (**Samar wood / حطب السمر** or **Ghada wood / حطب الغضا**);\n    - **The Dual Thermodynamic Stack**:\n      - Bottom level: An open pot of seasoned Basmati rice and water sits at the base;\n      - Top level: Marinated whole lamb or goat suspended on a metal wire rack directly above the rice;\n      - The pit is sealed airtight with wet burlap bags and desert sand for 2 to 3 hours;\n    - As the meat roasts in the sealed radiant convection heat, its aromatic juices and savory fats constantly drip directly onto the simmering rice below, infusing every grain with unctuous smoky flavor;\n- **Al-Madhbi (المظبي)**: Meat salted and grilled directly on smooth, heated river stones (*Al-Radf*) over glowing embers.",
