         "presentation": {
-            "explanation": "文法構造および実用会話表現の体系的詳細解説（Comprehensive Japanese Linguistic Architecture）:\n本レッスンでは、日本語の統語構造、敬語表現体系、および語用論的ニュアンスについて体系的かつ実践的に学習します。\n【主な学習項目と統語規則】：\n１．主語・目的語・述語の語順および格助詞（は、が、を、に、で、へ、より、から、まで）の厳格な使い分けと文脈に応じた省略規則。\n２．動詞および形容詞の活用体系（未然形・連用形・終止形・連体形・仮定形・命令形）とテ形接続・タ形接続における音便変化（イ音便・撥音便・促音便）。\n３．敬語表現（丁寧語「です・ます」、尊敬語「お～になる」、謙譲語「お～する・申す・伺う」）の場面別使い分けおよびビジネス対話マナー。\n４．日常会話、公的文書、学術論文における自然な談話構成法と接続詞の適切な運用。\n\n【解説と文脈理解 (English Grammatical Gloss)】:\n文法構造および実用会話表現の詳細解説（Japanese Grammatical Architecture）:\n本レッスンでは、日本語の統語構造、敬語表現体系、および語用論的ニュアンスについて体系的に学習します。\n【主な学習項目】：\n１．主語・目的語・述語の語順および助詞（は、が、を、に、で、へ、より）の厳密な使い分け。\n２．動詞の活用形（未然形・連用形・終止形・連体形・仮定形・命令形）とテ形・タ形の接続規則。\n３．待遇表現（丁寧語・尊敬語・謙譲語）の場面別使い分けおよびビジネス対話マナー。\n４．日常会話および公的場面における自然な談話構造の習得。\n\n【解説と文脈理解 (Grammatical Gloss)】:\n文法解説と実践的対話表現（Japanese Grammatical Architecture）:\n本レッスンでは、日本語の語順（主語・目的語・述語）、助詞の正確な使い分け（は・が・を・に・で）、および敬語体系（丁寧語・尊敬語・謙譲語）のニュアンスを深く学び、実際の文脈で自然に運用できる能力を養います。\n\nThe New National Theatre Tokyo (NNTT) and the contemporary operatic ecosystem in Japan:\n- **The Architectural & Operatic Crown: New National Theatre, Tokyo (新国立劇場 - NNTT - Opened October 1997 in Hatsudai, Shibuya)**:\n  - Japan's premier national center for the performing arts (Opera, Ballet, Contemporary Dance, and Spoken Drama);\n  - **The Opera House (オペラパレス / Opera Palace)**: 1,814-seat traditional proscenium acoustic hall with a 4-stage cross-shaped layout (main stage, rear stage, left and right wing stages), allowing complete set shifts in seconds;\n- Artistic Leadership & Global Prestige:\n  - Led by internationally acclaimed Maestro **Kazushi Ōno (大野和士)** (former Music Director of Brussels Royal Opera La Monnaie, Opéra de Lyon, and Barcelona Symphony);\n  - Commissions ambitious new Japanese contemporary operas (e.g. *A Midsummer Night's Dream*, *Silence* based on Shūsaku Endō);\n- The Two Pillars of Japanese Opera Companies:\n  - **Tokyo Nikikai Opera Theatre (東京二期会 - Founded 1952)** & **Fujiwara Opera (藤原歌劇団 - Founded 1934 by Yoshie Fujiwara)**;\n  - Co-producing world premieres with the Royal Opera House Covent Garden, Vienna State Opera, and Metropolitan Opera.",
+            "explanation": "The New National Theatre Tokyo (NNTT) and the contemporary operatic ecosystem in Japan:\n- **The Architectural & Operatic Crown: New National Theatre, Tokyo (新国立劇場 - NNTT - Opened October 1997 in Hatsudai, Shibuya)**:\n  - Japan's premier national center for the performing arts (Opera, Ballet, Contemporary Dance, and Spoken Drama);\n  - **The Opera House (オペラパレス / Opera Palace)**: 1,814-seat traditional proscenium acoustic hall with a 4-stage cross-shaped layout (main stage, rear stage, left and right wing stages), allowing complete set shifts in seconds;\n- Artistic Leadership & Global Prestige:\n  - Led by internationally acclaimed Maestro **Kazushi Ōno (大野和士)** (former Music Director of Brussels Royal Opera La Monnaie, Opéra de Lyon, and Barcelona Symphony);\n  - Commissions ambitious new Japanese contemporary operas (e.g. *A Midsummer Night's Dream*, *Silence* based on Shūsaku Endō);\n- The Two Pillars of Japanese Opera Companies:\n  - **Tokyo Nikikai Opera Theatre (東京二期会 - Founded 1952)** & **Fujiwara Opera (藤原歌劇団 - Founded 1934 by Yoshie Fujiwara)**;\n  - Co-producing world premieres with the Royal Opera House Covent Garden, Vienna State Opera, and Metropolitan Opera.",
