e grains harmonize perfectly with the fish fat on the tongue;\n  - **Classic Edomae Preservations**:\n    - **Zuke (漬け)**: Marinating lean tuna (*Maguro akami*) in hot sake, mirin, and soy sauce;\n    - **Shime (締め)**: Curing oily fish (*Kohada / Shime-saba*) in salt and vinegar;\n    - **Ni-anago (煮穴子)**: Braising sea eel until meltingly tender, glazed with a sweet reduction sauce (**Tsume / 煮詰め**);\n  - Documented globally in David Gelb's film *Jiro Dreams of Sushi* (2011) starring **Jiro Ono (小野二郎)** at Sukiyabashi Jiro.",
